Q58 (Original Q32) — Map host port to container port

# Host port 8082 maps to container port 80
sudo docker run -d --name port-demo -p 8082:80 nginx

sudo docker port port-demo
sudo docker ps

# Open http://localhost:8082
sudo docker stop port-demo
sudo docker rm port-demo

Syntax: -p HOST_PORT:CONTAINER_PORT.

Q59 (Original Q36) — Run Redis and inspect/execute commands

sudo docker pull redis
sudo docker run -d --name redis-lab redis
sudo docker ps
sudo docker inspect redis-lab

# Run Redis CLI inside the container
sudo docker exec -it redis-lab redis-cli
# At the Redis prompt:
PING
SET labkey "hello"
GET labkey
