sudo docker logs redis-lab
sudo docker stop redis-lab
sudo docker rm redis-lab

Q60 (Original Q44) — Run a database container and view status/logs

Use PostgreSQL with a disposable lab password only. Do not use a real or reused password.

sudo docker pull postgres:16
sudo docker run -d --name postgres-lab \
  -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=LabOnly123 \
  -e POSTGRES_DB=labdb \
  postgres:16

sudo docker ps -a
sudo docker logs postgres-lab
sudo docker inspect postgres-lab

# Clean up after demonstration
sudo docker stop postgres-lab
sudo docker rm postgres-lab

This example does not publish the database port to the host. It demonstrates container status and logs without exposing the database externally.

